    "created_at": "2019-05-14T13:02:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-14T13:02:13Z",
    "body": "@annevk The issue at hand that causes both the host and JS to coordinate agents is that JS wishes to impose a fairness constraint in `Atomics.wait` and `Atomics.waitAsync`. It would be bug prone to leave the scheduling algorithm to the host in all cases, or split the algorithm between JS and the host. And besides, we want it to be fair in the same way for all hosts. Any recommendations here?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/492227786/reactions",
